# CYD UI layout rules (320×240)

All screens in `src/ui.cpp` must follow this grid. **Body content never overlaps the footer touch zone.**

## Zones (Y axis)

| Zone | Y range | Purpose |
|------|---------|---------|
| Header | 0–35 | Title, SCAN, status bar, top CANCEL |
| Body | 36–205 | Lists, keyboard, panels, action buttons |
| Footer | 206–239 | Single nav row (`drawFooterBack`, touch `y >= UI_FOOTER_TOP`) |

Constants live in `src/config.h` (`UI_HEADER_BOTTOM`, `UI_BODY_BOTTOM`, `UI_FOOTER_TOP`, etc.).

## Rules

1. **One footer per screen** — never stack a footer on top of keyboard keys or list rows.
2. **Password screen** — no footer; only top-left CANCEL. Keyboard bottom row ends above `UI_FOOTER_TOP`.
3. **Scrollable lists** — use right-side ▲/▼ buttons (`drawScrollBtn`) when items exceed visible rows; show page indicator.
4. **Touch handlers** — must match draw zones; check footer before body; use same constants as draw.
5. **Text** — truncate long SSIDs/URLs; prefer 2-line banners over 3-line blocks in 32px height.
6. **Main menu** — max 2 button rows; bottom row bottom ≤ 220; preview capped at 2 host + 2 Wi-Fi lines.

## Before shipping UI changes

- Grep for hardcoded `y=210`, `y=226`, `hitFooterBack` paired with overlapping draw rects.
- Run `scripts/test_boot_ux.py` on hardware after touch-target changes.
